# Backlog 64 (fixed 0.4), in the genre that pays for it: an
# RFC-faithful state machine is the figure most likely to be BOTH pinned (the
# source drawing's arrangement is part of what it says) and self-looped (the
# events whose defined outcome is "stay put"). Until 0.4 it could not
# be both: pinning any state degenerated its self-transition to a zero-length
# line at the state's centre and printed the trigger across the state's name,
# so a figure had to choose between the source's arrangement and the source's
# self-transitions. Three pinned states, three inter-state transitions and
# three self-transitions; all three loops now draw.
#
# The model is what this golden pins. The DRAWING — every self-loop's path
# length and its label's clearance from the state's own name — is asserted by
# tools/shape-check.js on the v0.1 twin, conformance/cases/371-pin-self-edge-loop.fd.
figdown 0.2 statechart
title "Pinned states still draw their self-transitions"
state down "DOWN"
state init "INIT"
state up "UP"
transition down -[rx Down]-> init
transition init -[rx Init, rx Up]-> up
transition up -[Detect expired]-> down
transition down -[rx Up]-> down
transition init -[rx Down]-> init
transition up -[rx Init]-> up
layout
pin down at=(220,40) width=110 height=56
pin init at=(60,200) width=110 height=56
pin up at=(380,200) width=110 height=56
